#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063" :question/math-academy-id "e-4810" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAb_{1} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{bmatrix} \\ne 0\\cdot \\\\\nAb_{2} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} = 0✓ \\\\\nAb_{3} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix} \\ne 0\\cdot\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e38db5fa-1753-5176-bb5e-a077ea63ddec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4812" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A)$." :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A)$, then we must have\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAb &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 + 2k - 12 \\\\ -6 + 3k - 3 \\\\ 12 - 6k + 6\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{2k - 6 = 0; 3k - 9 = 0; - 6k + 18 = 0\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "1e59cd29-ea54-5b90-8215-60c81d1b6dbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4814" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\textrm{Null}(A)$." :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1} &:=\\frac{1}{4}R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{x_{1} - 3x_{2} = 0; x_{2} = 0\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0$. Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} - 3x_{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx_{1} - 3(0) &= 0 \\\\\nx_{1} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{\\mathbf{0} \\right\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a54c0add-73d3-59e6-a39b-e7a418e46c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}2x_{2} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}: x_{2} ∈ R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118043} {:answer/id #uuid "b48c2cfd-7c3f-5010-8056-b39ed91a19a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} \\\\ -3x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}: x_{2} ∈ R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118044} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a55a82-bfd9-5b46-9246-8dad3eac99c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118045} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4b3f11-a561-57ec-addc-83ecdc021aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}-2x_{2} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}: x_{2} ∈ R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118046} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9defd2-5053-560e-9cb1-5d3d60c073a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} \\\\ 2x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}: x_{2} ∈ R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc4b3f11-a561-57ec-addc-83ecdc021aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}-2x_{2} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}: x_{2} ∈ R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118046} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e11750b-6ea3-587d-9b5b-5e604b2b3b7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118042}] :question/id #uuid "dcd84fb5-e504-5016-bbba-4d8edb437f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34333" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $Null(A)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :k